    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nThis is a rare and wonderful opportunity to acquire an elegant and imposing five-bedroom late Victorian semi-detached residence dating from c.1888, occupying an excellent position on the sunny south side of Temple Gardens, one of Dublin's most prestigious and sought-after residential roads. Set well back from the road on mature private gardens extending to approximately 0.27 acres, this is a home of exceptional charm, character and distinction.\nNumber 22, or Kincora as it is named, forms part of the historic Palmerston Estate, developed by renowned Dublin property developer and builder Henry Coghlan. One of the first 6 homes of this prestigious Victorian and Edwardian enclave, it retains the name bestowed by Coghlan over 135 years ago, offering a rare link to its heritage. Kincora reflects the craftsmanship, scale and enduring quality of the Victorian era, perfectly defining Temple Gardens. A quiet road of just 26 houses, featuring a mix of very fine detached and semi-detached residences, it is tucked away between the broad sweep of Palmerston Road and quieter Merton Road running along the Luas track to Cowper. \nExtending to approximately 289 sq.m. (3,111 sq.ft.), this beautiful family home has been lovingly maintained over the last 31 years by its current owners who have carefully preserved its wonderful architectural heritage both inside and out. The impressive interior is rich in period detail, including magnificent ceiling heights of approximately 3.8m at ground floor level, ornate cornicing, original joinery, sash windows and elegant fireplaces, all synonymous with the grandeur of the Victorian era. Large windows flood the beautifully proportioned rooms with natural light, creating a warm and welcoming atmosphere throughout.\nThe accommodation is arranged over two floors with a top return and offers a superb balance of elegant reception rooms and generous double bedroom space. A gracious entrance hall leads to three elegant reception rooms, each with original character and ideal for both day-to-day family living and entertaining. At the heart of the home is a spacious kitchen/dining room overlooking the rear garden, complemented by a practical utility room. Upstairs there are five generous double bedrooms, together with a family bathroom, shower room and guest WC.\nOne of the property's outstanding features is its magnificent south-facing rear garden, extending to approximately 133 ft. in length a rare find in Dublin 6. Wonderfully private and beautifully mature, it is laid out primarily in lawn and enhanced by an abundance of specimen trees, shrubs and flowering plants, providing year-round colour and interest This garden offers exceptional seclusion together with significant potential to further extend the existing accommodation, subject to planning permission. A large garage to the rear, with valuable vehicular access onto Palmerston Lane, presents exciting future possibilities, including potential mews development, again subject to planning permission.\nTo the front, the mature landscaped garden provides generous off-street parking for several cars, a highly sought-after feature in this prime Dublin 6 location.\nThe location is second to none. Just two miles from St Stephen's Green, Temple Gardens enjoys an almost unparalleled sense of convenience. The Luas at Cowper is within a short stroll, while the villages of Rathmines, Ranelagh, Rathgar and Dartry offer an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, specialist shops, parks and recreational amenities. Palmerston Park, a much-loved local landmark, is at the heart of this vibrant community and neighbourhood. Sporting facilities nearby include Milltown Golf Club, Brookfield Tennis Club and Dartry Health Club.\nThe area is also renowned for its exceptional choice of schools, with many of Dublin's finest junior and senior schools within easy reach, including Alexandra College, Gonzaga College, St Mary's College, Muckross College, Sandford National School, Sandford Park School, Kildare Place School, Scoil Bhríde, Stratford College and Zion National School.\nKincora, 22 Temple Gardens offers a most desirable combination of period elegance, practical and generous living and bedroom space, magnificent gardens, valuable off-street parking and an unrivalled Dublin 6 address. It is an exceptional family home, ready to be enjoyed and loved by a new family"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nHall Level - \n\n\nEntrance Porch - \nDouble doors with glazed panels lead to the porch with tiled floor. Fan light. Double doors with feature stained glass side panels leading to:\n\nReception Hallway - \n3.8m high ceiling with ornate cornice, centre rose and dado rail, polished timber floor, antique radiator, archway, understairs storage.\n\nDrawing Room - \nBay window overlooking front garden, sash windows, open fire with painted mantlepiece and brick, brass and marble surround and hearth, elaborate cornice, centre rose and dado rail, polished timber floor, and antique radiator.\n\nLiving Room - \nTwo large sash windows, marble mantlepiece with marble and brass surround and hearth, flanked by fitted cabinets on both sides, elaborate plasterwork and picture rail, polished timber floor, antique radiator.\n\nFamily Room - \nOpen fire with marble mantlepiece, tiled heath and surround, flanked by cabinets on both sides, cornice and centre rose, French doors to rear garden.\n\nGuest WC - \nWC, Armitage Shanks handbasin on vanity unit, sash window overlooking rear garden, tiled floor, cornice, recessed lighting, built-in storage.\n\nSteps down to door into - \n\n\nKitchen / Dining Room - \nL-shaped room with large range of hand-painted kitchen units (colour: intense rich olive from Messel No39), incorporating Belfast sink, Bosch dishwasher, Electrolux fridge, Brittania range cooker with 6 ring gas hob, two ovens and chef hob, extractor fan, island unit with additional storage, black marble countertops, large pantry, double doors to rear garden, tiled floor throughout kitchen and dining area, sash window and 3 Velux windows, recessed lights and pendants over island.\n\nUtility Room - \nFloor to ceiling storage units, sink unit, countertop and tiled splashback, plumbed for washing machine and dryer, sash window.\n\nFirst Return - \n\n\nBuilt in storage / window seat - \nWith sash window behind\n\nBedroom 1 - \nGenerous double to rear, sash window overlooking rear garden, cornice\n\nFirst Floor - \nLanding with cornice\n\nBedroom 2 (front) - \nTwo sash windows, large range of fitted wardrobes, cornice, polished timber floor, open fireplace with painted mantlepiece and slate hearth\n\nBedroom 3 / Main bedroom (front) - \nTwo sash windows, cornice, polished timber floor, open fireplace with painted mantlepiece and slate hearth, door to:\n\nDressing Room - \nSash window with plantation shutter, large range of fitted wardrobes, polished timber floor, cornice.\n\nBedroom 4 - \nDouble to rear, sash window, painted timber floor, cornice.\n\nShower Room - \nSash window with plantation shutters, WC, Duravit wash hand basin, mirrored cabinet, shower cubicle with wall mounted shower, storage press, tiled floor and walls, recessed lights, recessed shelving, heated towel rail.\n\nSecond Return - \nSash window, fitted wardrobes, painted timber floor, attic hatch\n\nBedroom 5 - \nSash window, fitted wardrobes, painted timber floor, attic hatch\n\nFamily Bathroom - \nFully tiled, wc, wash hand basin on vanity unit, Duravit bath with screen and wall mounted shower, sash window with plantation shutters, heated towel rail and underfloor heating , recessed lights.\n\nOutside - \nKincora enjoys gardens of 0.27 acres (approx.) and they are both a joy and rarity to behold. A traditional railed front garden with hedging and mature shrubs and trees, is laid out in lawn and gravel driveway with ample parking for several cars with a discreet bin area. A gated side passage leads to the rear gardens. Truly stunning, the lush rear garden of L.133 ft (approx.), enjoys a sunny southerly orientation. Laid out in lawn with wide borders well stocked with a wide selection of mature shrubs, trees, beautiful apple tree and seasonal flowers. A large patio is located off the kitchen and living room and spans the full width of the house the perfect spot for outdoor dining and entertaining. The rear elevation is part clad in purple-flowering wisteria. At the base of this mature, private garden is a large garage, which measures 40m x 17m offering vehicular access to Palmerston Lane, an established mews lane with access to Milltown Path.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>An elegant and imposing late Victorian semi-detached home</li><li>Sits perfectly on majestic gardens of 0.27acre approx </li><li>Private rear garden measures L133 ft approx.</li><li>Enjoys a sunny southerly orientation to rear </li><li>Well appointed, light-filled accommodation of 289 sqm / 3111 sqft approx</li><li>Wonderful balance of three gracious reception rooms and five double bedrooms</li><li>A much-loved and cared for family home, perfectly positioned on this quiet tree-lined avenue, one of Dublin's most sought-after roads</li><li>Retains a wealth of original and exquisite period details</li><li>Large garage to rear with vehicular access to Palmerston Lane - an established mews laneway - offering mews potential subject to planning permission</li><li>Close to Cowper and Beechwood Luas stops</li><li>Close to local shopping on Dunville Avenue, Upper Rathmines Road and all amenities of Rathmines and Ranelagh</ul>"
      },
      {
